claude-v1:
 Here is the LaTeX code to generate that plot:

```latex
\usepackage{pgfplots}

\begin{document}
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[
xlabel={x},
ylabel={sin(x)},
xmin=-2*pi, xmax=2*pi, 
xtick={-2*pi,-pi,0,pi,2*pi},
xticklabel={-2\pi,-\pi,0,\pi,2\pi},
ylabel style={yshift=0.5ex},
axis line style={->}, 
width=0.8\textwidth,
height=0.6\textwidth,
]

\addplot[blue,line width=1.5pt] 
table[x=-2*pi:2*pi:0.1] {sin(x)};

\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{document}
```

This loads the pgfplots package, defines a tikzpicture environment, and within that an axis environment to set the axis labels, range, tick marks, etc. The \addplot command plots the sine curve in the specified blue color and line width. The table option is used to give the (x, y) points from -2pi to 2pi with a step size of 0.1.

vicuna-13b:
Here is a LaTeX code for plotting a sine function using pgfplots package:
```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{pgfplots}

\begin{document}

\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[
    xlabel={$x$},
    ylabel={$\sin(x)$},
    xmin=-2*pi, xmax=2*pi,
    ymin=-1, ymax=1,
    restrict y to domain=-1:1,
    enlargelimits=true,
    enlarge y limits={abs=1},
    samples=100,
    axis lines=middle,
    clip=false,
    legend style={
        at={(0.5,-0.15)},
        anchor=north,
        legend columns=2,
        font=\small,
        draw=none,
        fill=none,
    },
    ]
    \addplot[
        color=blue,
        line width=1.5pt,
        domain=-2*pi:2*pi,
        samples=100,
        restrict y to domain=-1:1,
        ] {sin(x)};
    \addlegendentry{$\sin(x)$}
    \end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}

\end{document}
```
This code will produce a plot of the sine function with the specified domain, range, and line width. The plot is drawn using the `addplot` command and the `sin` function is used for the plot's data. The `legend` command is used to add a legend to the plot, which labels the plot as "sin(x)".

input:
#include <stdio.h>

unsigned long long factorial_recursive(int n) {
    if (n == 0) {
        return 1;
    } else {
        return n * factorial_recursive(n - 1);
    }
}

unsigned long long factorial_iterative(int n) {
    unsigned long long result = 1;
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        result *= i;
    }
    return result;
}

int main() {
    int number;
    unsigned long long recursive_result, iterative_result;

    printf("Enter a positive integer: ");
    scanf("%d", &number);

    if (number < 0) {
        printf("Invalid input. Please enter a positive integer.\n");
        return 1;
    }

    recursive_result = factorial_recursive(number);
    iterative_result = factorial_iterative(number);

    printf("Factorial (Recursive): %llu\n", recursive_result);
    printf("Factorial (Iterative): %llu\n", iterative_result);

    return 0;
}

